    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0726" n="705" xml:id="pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.811/8–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Yugoslavia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-16T13:00:00-04:00">August 16, 1948—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>495. Dudel 45. Reference your Niact Deldu 71 Aug 14, full powers went forward you
                    sometime ago as general formality. In view decision not to sign convention these
                    should now be disregarded.</p>
                <p>Dept believes final act should not be signed even if no miscellaneous
                    resolutions, protocols, and Soviet convention attached. Dept may wish to
                    denounce whole proceedings later, therefore would prefer no signature of final
                    act.</p>
                <p>Dept assumes tel from Paris sent Dept as 4216; and rptd Belgrade as 104 Aug
                        14,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d455-f1"/> supersedes views expressed Dept by
                    French Embassy Aug 14 reported to you by niact 494 Dudel 44.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d455-f1" n="1" xml:id="d455-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Ambassador Caffery reported from Paris in this telegram that the
                    French Foreign Ministry had stated that it believed that the point of view of
                    the United States, rather than that of the British, was correct and that it
                    would so inform the French delegation in Belgrade. (840.811/8–1448)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
